# No Emojis Rule

## Purpose and Scope

This rule enforces a complete prohibition on emoji usage in code, design elements, and content. It ensures professional consistency, accessibility compliance, and cross-platform compatibility across all project files. The rule applies to all code files, content files, and design elements to maintain the professional brewery brand aesthetic.

## Standards and Requirements

### Absolute Prohibition
- **NEVER** use emoji characters (🕒, 👥, 🐕, etc.) in any code files
- **NEVER** use emojis as icons, decorative elements, or visual enhancements
- **NEVER** include emojis in component text, titles, or descriptions
- **NEVER** use emojis in CSS content properties or pseudo-elements
- **NEVER** use emojis in markdown files, documentation, or comments

### Professional Standards
- Maintain professional business website appearance
- Ensure cross-platform rendering consistency
- Support accessibility requirements and screen readers
- Align with brewery brand aesthetic and tone

### Alternative Solutions
- Use proper SVG icons or icon fonts for visual elements
- Implement text-based design elements and typography
- Rely on CSS gradients, shadows, and spacing for visual hierarchy
- Use color, typography, and layout for visual appeal

## Examples

### Good Examples

```tsx
// Professional component with proper icons
import { Clock, Users, Dog } from 'phosphor-react';

export function InfoSection() {
  return (
    <div className={styles.infoSection}>
      <div className={styles.infoItem}>
        <Clock className={styles.icon} />
        <h3>Kitchen Hours</h3>
      </div>
      <div className={styles.infoItem}>
        <Users className={styles.icon} />
        <p>Family-friendly environment</p>
      </div>
      <div className={styles.infoItem}>
        <Dog className={styles.icon} />
        <p>We welcome well-behaved dogs</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  );
}
```

```css
/* Professional CSS without emojis */
.infoIcon::before {
  content: "⏰"; /* ❌ Don't use emoji */
}

.infoIcon::before {
  content: ""; /* ✅ Use background image or icon font */
  background-image: url('/icons/clock.svg');
  background-size: contain;
}
```

```tsx
// Professional content without emojis
<h2>Welcome to Broken Loop Brewing</h2>
<p>Experience craft beer excellence in a welcoming atmosphere</p>
```

### Bad Examples

```tsx
// ❌ Don't use emojis in components
<div className={styles.infoIcon}>🕒</div>
<h3>Kitchen Hours 🍽️</h3>
<p>We welcome dogs 🐕</p>
```

*Fails: Uses emoji characters which are unprofessional and inaccessible.*

```css
/* ❌ Don't use emojis in CSS */
.icon::before {
  content: "🍺";
}
```

*Fails: Uses emoji in CSS content property which can cause rendering issues.*

```tsx
// ❌ Don't use emojis in comments or documentation
// 🚀 This component handles user authentication
// ⚠️ TODO: Add error handling
```

*Fails: Uses emojis in code comments which is unprofessional.*

## Implementation Guidelines

### Code Review Process
- Always review code for emoji usage before committing
- Check all file types: TypeScript, JavaScript, CSS, Markdown
- Remove any emojis found immediately
- Replace with appropriate alternatives

### Icon Implementation
```tsx
// Use proper icon libraries
import { 
  Clock, 
  Users, 
  Dog, 
  Beer, 
  MapPin, 
  Phone 
} from 'phosphor-react';

// Or use SVG components
const ClockIcon = () => (
  <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor">
    <path d="M12 2C6.48 2 2 6.48 2 12s4.48 10 10 10 10-4.48 10-10S17.52 2 12 2zm-2 15l-5-5 1.41-1.41L10 14.17l7.59-7.59L19 8l-9 9z"/>
  </svg>
);
```

### Content Guidelines
- Use descriptive text instead of emojis
- Implement proper typography hierarchy
- Use color and spacing for visual emphasis
- Focus on professional tone and messaging

### Accessibility Considerations
- Ensure all icons have proper alt text or aria-labels
- Use semantic HTML elements
- Maintain proper color contrast ratios
- Support screen reader navigation

### Cross-Platform Testing
- Test rendering across different browsers
- Verify display on various operating systems
- Check mobile device compatibility
- Ensure consistent appearance in different locales

